\"/></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(96.615356 29.648) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" d=\"M 2131 4813 Q 2598 4813 2950 4649 Q 3302 4486 3500 4192 Q 3699 3898 3699 3507 Q 3699 3206 3545 2969 Q 3392 2733 3053 2496 Q 2957 2432 3046 2394 Q 3341 2278 3529 2112 Q 3718 1946 3814 1731 Q 3910 1517 3910 1261 Q 3910 858 3683 557 Q 3456 256 3053 96 Q 2650 -64 2112 -64 Q 1587 -64 1196 83 Q 806 230 598 508 Q 390 787 390 1178 Q 390 1517 560 1789 Q 730 2061 1120 2304 Q 1197 2349 1200 2377 Q 1203 2406 1126 2445 Q 947 2547 809 2688 Q 672 2829 595 3014 Q 518 3200 518 3437 Q 518 3827 720 4137 Q 922 4448 1286 4630 Q 1651 4813 2131 4813 L 2131 4813 z\nM 2138 4365 Q 1850 4365 1613 4249 Q 1376 4134 1238 3939 Q 1101 3744 1101 3488 Q 1101 2906 1760 2758 L 2419 2605 Q 2509 2579 2633 2649 Q 2758 2720 2880 2854 Q 3002 2989 3078 3161 Q 3155 3334 3155 3514 Q 3155 3891 2880 4128 Q 2605 4365 2138 4365 L 2138 4365 z\nM 2144 384 Q 2675 384 2988 614 Q 3302 845 3302 1235 Q 3302 1530 3142 1715 Q 2982 1901 2624 1984 L 1792 2189 Q 1696 2214 1555 2153 Q 1414 2093 1273 1961 Q 1133 1830 1033 1648 Q 934 1466 934 1248 Q 934 838 1244 611 Q 1555 384 2144 384 L 2144 384 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(65.40625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(208.940656 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\" transform=\"translate(66.09375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(321.324707 46.208) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" d=\"M 1869 -58 Q 1626 -58 1424 -6 Q 1222 45 1062 134 Q 902 224 784 336 Q 666 448 582 563 Q 570 589 566 617 Q 563 646 602 666 L 966 813 Q 998 832 1020 816 Q 1043 800 1062 774 Q 1197 608 1389 505 Q 1581 403 1869 403 Q 2323 403 2611 627 Q 2899 851 3036 1238 Q 3174 1626 3174 2112 Q 3174 2221 3158 2249 Q 3142 2278 3066 2240 Q 2822 2118 2550 2016 Q 2278 1914 1894 1914 Q 1414 1914 1065 2096 Q 717 2278 534 2592 Q 352 2906 352 3302 Q 352 3757 569 4096 Q 787 4435 1164 4620 Q 1542 4806 2003 4806 Q 2554 4806 2954 4528 Q 3354 4250 3571 3722 Q 3789 3194 3789 2445 Q 3789 1664 3555 1104 Q 3322 544 2896 243 Q 2470 -58 1869 -58 L 1869 -58 z\nM 1965 2362 Q 2150 2362 2348 2403 Q 2547 2445 2732 2521 Q 2918 2598 3046 2688 Q 3123 2739 3148 2793 Q 3174 2848 3174 2963 Q 3174 3187 3104 3430 Q 3034 3674 2890 3885 Q 2746 4096 2525 4227 Q 2304 4358 2003 4358 Q 1709 4358 1472 4224 Q 1235 4090 1097 3856 Q 960 3622 960 3328 Q 960 3059 1085 2838 Q 1210 2618 1434 2490 Q 1658 2362 1965 2362 L 1965 2362 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" transform=\"translate(64.90625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p561cd55998\"><rect x=\"41.248156\" y=\"10.824\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Units per hour by step","note":null},"answer":"<p>Finishing is slowest: 49 × 1,820 = 89.2k units; after 95% yield, <b>84.7k</b>, against demand of 105k.</p>"},{"q":"A second lacquer booth raises finishing speed by 22% for $450k. What does it deliver?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Finishing: 59.8/hour, but cutting (58/hour) is now the bottleneck: 105.6k units, <b>100.3k good units</b>.</p> <p>Extra: 15.6k × $24 = $373k a year; payback 1.2 years. Still 4.7k short of demand.</p>"},{"q":"Cutting could be made 10% faster for $150k (a faster saw and better panel loading). What if Cascade does both?","exhibit":{"kind":"table","headers":["","Today","+ lacquer booth","+ booth and faster saw"],"rows":[["Bottleneck","Finishing","Cutting","Finishing"],["Good units (k)","84.7","100.3","103.4"],["Extra contribution vs today ($k)","—","373","447"]],"title":"Exhibit 2 · Options compared","note":null,"align":["l","r","r","r"],"boldLast":false},"answer":"<p>Cutting: 63.8/hour; finishing at 59.8 is the bottleneck again: 108.8k units, <b>103.4k good</b>, just below demand.</p> <p>The cutting upgrade adds a further 3.1k units: $74k a year for $150k, a payback of <b>2.0 years</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the two changes work as a pair. On its own, the booth leaves Cascade short; together they nearly close the gap for $600k, paying back in 1.3 years.</p>"}],"reco":"Do both: add the second lacquer booth and speed up cutting. The booth alone moves the bottleneck to cutting and leaves Cascade about 4.7k units short; with a 10% faster saw, output reaches about 103.4k good units against demand of 105k, adding about $447k a year and paying back the $600k in 1.3 years. Risk: both projects must land together, so plan the installs in the same summer shutdown. Next step: get firm quotes and installation dates.","great":["Checks the bottleneck after each change","Sequences investments by where capacity is limited","Compares output with demand at each step","Recommends the combination, with a payback"],"id":48,"slug":"cascade-furniture"}